{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01UDrPJm8z7s8djiXrNoAmhG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Rust translation of the C library in `c_src/`.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! Public ABI surface (from `nm -D` on the C shared object):\n4\t//!   * `md5_digest`\n5\t//!\n6\t//! Header (`include/lib.h`) declares:\n7\t//! ```c\n8\t//! typedef uint8_t  tflac_u8;\n9\t//! typedef uint32_t tflac_u32;\n10\t//!\n11\t//! struct tflac_md5 {\n12\t//!     tflac_u32 a;\n13\t//!     tflac_u32 b;\n14\t//!     tflac_u32 c;\n15\t//!     tflac_u32 d;\n16\t//! };\n17\t//! typedef struct tflac_md5 tflac_md5;\n18\t//!\n19\t//! void md5_digest(const tflac_md5 *m, tflac_u8 out[16]);\n20\t//! ```\n21\t//!\n22\t//! There are no namespace-renaming preprocessor macros in the header, so the\n23\t//! linker symbol name is exactly `md5_digest`.\n24\t\n25\t#![allow(non_camel_case_types)]\n26\t\n27\t/// `typedef uint8_t tflac_u8;`\n28\tpub type tflac_u8 = u8;\n29\t\n30\t/// `typedef uint32_t tflac_u32;`\n31\tpub type tflac_u32 = u32;\n32\t\n33\t/// `struct tflac_md5` — layout-compatible with the C struct (four\n34\t/// naturally-aligned 32-bit words, no padding).\n35\t#[repr(C)]\n36\t#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]\n37\tpub struct tflac_md5 {\n38\t    pub a: tflac_u32,\n39\t    pub b: tflac_u32,\n40\t    pub c: tflac_u32,\n41\t    pub d: tflac_u32,\n42\t}\n43\t\n44\t/// Serialize the four MD5 state words little-endian into `out[0..16]`.\n45\t///\n46\t/// Faithful translation of:\n47\t///\n48\t/// ```c\n49\t/// void md5_digest(const tflac_md5 *m, tflac_u8 out[16]) {\n50\t///     out[0] = (tflac_u8)(m->a);\n51\t///     out[1] = (tflac_u8)(m->a >> 8);\n52\t///     ...\n53\t///     out[15] = (tflac_u8)(m->d >> 24);\n54\t/// }\n55\t/// ```\n56\t///\n57\t/// Exactly like the C original, no null / alignment validation is performed on\n58\t/// either argument; passing invalid pointers is undefined behaviour in both\n59\t/// versions.\n60\t///\n61\t/// # Safe